<% content_for :title, "Carousel CSV import and export" %>
<h1>Carousel CSV import and export</h1>
<p>Download the carousel spreadsheet, make your changes, then upload or paste it here to review before saving.</p>
<p>Figures, seats, and placement history are not included in the spreadsheet.</p>
<p><%= link_to "Download carousel CSV", export_carousel_csv_path, class: "button" %></p>
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Before importing</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Edit existing carousels:</strong> Keep their ID, slug, and updated_at cells as they are. Leaving a row out will not delete the carousel.</li>
    <li><strong>Add carousels:</strong> Add a new row and leave ID, slug, and updated_at blank. A new carousel's status will be unknown unless you provide one.</li>
    <li><strong>Leave or clear a value:</strong> A blank cell leaves an existing value unchanged. To remove an optional value, enter <code>__CLEAR__</code> in that cell.</li>
    <li><strong>Review before saving:</strong> The preview shows your changes, errors, and possible duplicates. Nothing is saved until you confirm.</li>
  </ol>
  <details>
    <summary>More spreadsheet details</summary>
    <ul>
      <li>Save as UTF-8 CSV. Keep the column names, the csv_format column, and any apostrophes at the start of exported cells. These help protect spreadsheet text and make re-importing work.</li>
      <li>Use the maker IDs listed below. Add sources for published counts and ring research; ring columns A through F describe the individual rings.</li>
      <li>Existing layout dimensions cannot be changed here. Adding both dimensions to a carousel without a complete layout creates unknown seats.</li>
      <li>To save the literal text <code>__CLEAR__</code>, enter <code>\__CLEAR__</code> instead.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each import is limited to 1 MB, 5,000 rows, and 10,000 new seats. A preview is valid for 30 minutes.</p>
  </details>
  <p><%= link_to "Read the full import guide", editor_guide_path(anchor: "carousel-csv") %></p>
</section>
<%= render "form", csv_text: params[:csv_text] %>
<% if Maker.exists? %>
  <details>
    <summary>Maker IDs</summary>
    <table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Maker</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><% Maker.order(:name, :id).each do |maker| %><tr><td><%= maker.id %></td><td><%= maker.name %></td></tr><% end %></tbody>
    </table>
  </details>
<% end %>
